flatpkg runs unmodified Flatpak Linux applications on FreeBSD.

It is not a port of Flatpak and does not run FreeBSD applications: it
replaces exactly one layer, sandbox construction.  bubblewrap becomes a
per-launch jail(8), the OverlayFS and bind mounts become unionfs, nullfs
and tmpfs, the device binds become devfs rulesets, and the Flatpak runtime
tree itself - the Linux ELF binaries Flatpak ships - is the jail's
userland, executed by the FreeBSD Linuxulator.

Distribution is orchestrated, not reimplemented: the store is a real OSTree
repository driven by the real ostree binary.

The client is never setuid.  Every command is served over a Unix socket by a
root daemon that authenticates the caller with getpeereid(2) and drops to the
caller's uid before exec'ing the application.

WWW: https://github.com/Poiesys/flatpkg
